{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":88,"recorded_at":1780531400000171,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e64d12b9-3850-49e7-bf58-73a2eb2bcddc"},"task_id":"e64d12b9-3850-49e7-bf58-73a2eb2bcddc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e64d12b9-3850-49e7-bf58-73a2eb2bcddc","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cigate/doc.go`.\n1|// Package cigate implements the M0 continuous-conformance CI gates for the\n2|// security-primitives-and-conformance-ci story: historical and current\n3|// contract preservation, fixture-target derivation, and the\n4|// unsupported-capability advertisement check.\n5|//\n6|// It is a gate, not a second authority. Every behavior it constrains is\n7|// decided by an existing owner; this package only re-derives those decisions\n8|// from their owners and refuses drift:\n9|//\n10|//   - pinned contract versions stay in internal/specpin; the typed release\n11|//     projections stay in internal/catalog. VerifyContractPreservation\n12|//     requires the two authorities to agree exactly and fails closed on a\n13|//     version either side cannot account for;\n14|//   - platform capability availability stays in internal/secconftest probes.\n15|//     CheckAdvertisements takes probe outcomes as input and never defines a\n16|//     capability of its own;\n17|//   - fuzz entry points stay in internal/secconftest. FuzzTargets derives the\n18|//     committed target list from FuzzTargetEntry rather than retyping it.\n19|//\n20|// Normative scope: AX v0.5.0 Sections 16, 19.2-19.5, 20.2, Appendix D. The\n21|// Section 19.3 provider suites and Section 19.4 lifecycle cases outside\n22|// Section 16 are not driven here; CI runs them only where their owning\n23|// packages already implement them, and this gate claims nothing about the\n24|// rest.\n25|//\n26|// Stated bounds. The gates are read-only: they parse the pinned authorities\n27|// and repository text and write only their verdict to the caller. They mutate\n28|// no durable state, keep no cache, and carry no crash or idempotency surface\n29|// of their own; crash/idempotency evidence for the story is the secconftest\n30|// Transactor battery, which CI executes but which lives outside this package.\n31|// Availability is evaluated on the host that runs the check: a positive claim\n32|// about a capability available here is admitted even when the same sentence\n33|// would be refused on a host where the probe fails. Cross-host claim truth is\n34|// outside this gate. The advertisement scanner reads prose only; it classifies\n35|// sentences, not intent, and any sentence it cannot classify is refused rather\n36|// than ignored.\n37|//\n38|// Deliberate shape decision: this package ships no main package. Its library\n39|// entry points import internal/secconftest for the probe vocabulary, and\n40|// secconftest reads internal/specdoc, which the specdoc guard forbids any new\n41|// main from reaching (TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary and\n42|// TestModuleHasNoProductCommandYet). A cigate command would need either a\n43|// foreign allowlist widening or a second probe vocabulary, both of which this\n44|// story exists to refuse. CI therefore drives these gates through focused,\n45|// name-guarded go test selections; the guards prove the selection matched.\n46|package cigate"}}}
