{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c487","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":158,"recorded_at":1780531400000311,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"05d93a8b-7d6b-4383-864a-7445f6dfaeef"},"task_id":"05d93a8b-7d6b-4383-864a-7445f6dfaeef","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"05d93a8b-7d6b-4383-864a-7445f6dfaeef","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-4-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"cigate\\\\|capabilit\\\\|live probe\\\\|scanned against\\\\|fuzz\\\\|FuzzTargets\\\\|secconftest\\\" README.md | head -40\",\n  \"description\": \"Find README CI claims\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"11:contract, operation, capability-vocabulary, event, and error catalogs from\\n87:command, `doctor` result, conformance-target declaration, or runtime capability\\n126:mutates no durable state, and advertises no runtime capability.\\n157:availability claim, or runtime capability advertisement.\\n172:  -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n234:The v3 terminal capability vocabulary is derived from the pinned catalog's\\n236:property of the pinned Configuration catalog, so neither a new capability nor a\\n245:`required_capabilities` remains marked as contextual default provenance; this\\n279:runtime capability/backend availability. Existing selected roots are checked\\n378:Section 6.5 additionally names the `required_capabilities` default defect. See\\n404:availability, status, or capability claim, and the package is an internal M0\\n464:the Section 7.4 probe with its seven capability values (only\\n465:`available` may be `enabled`), the host-side capability gate\\n612:[`internal/secconftest`](internal/secconftest) is the test instrument\\n614:runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzz drivers, hostile\\n615:strings, and platform capability skips. It decides nothing itself —\\n659:witness gated on a probed capability. Capability probes (`symlink`,\\n661:capability — symlink create+Lstat, `mkfifo`+Lstat, `chmod 000`\\n675:Run the focused tests, race, coverage, and fuzz smoke with:\\n678:go test ./internal/secconftest -count=1\\n679:go test ./internal/secconftest -race -count=1\\n680:go test ./internal/secconftest -cover -count=1\\n681:go test ./internal/secconftest -run='^$' -fuzz='^FuzzCheckArgv$' -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n688:vector gates, not containment races; the env-name/redact fuzz pins\\n697:capability is advertised: the instrument cannot enable a platform\\n711:| Contract preservation | `tracecheck`, catalog freshness, focused `internal/cigate` contract gates | The pinned lock and the generated catalog agree on every historical and current contract version, and each gate selection matched its named test |\\n718:| Unsupported-capability claim check | README scanned against live probe verdicts | No unsupported capability is advertised: mentions resolve to probe, skip, gate, or test context, never to a positive availability claim about an unavailable capability |\\n722:[`internal/cigate`](internal/cigate) holds the CI-facing gate library:\\n725:fuzz-target derivation from the instrument's own target map, and the\\n726:advertisement check wired to the `internal/secconftest` probe set rather\\n910:replication, materialization, tombstone, capability, bridge, sync, or takeover\\n934:capability is claimed by this package.\\n1126:fuzz corpora, and `tracecheck` — still green, because 91 runtime refusal\\n1343:Native fuzz targets recursively attack malformed member syntax, duplicate\\n1355:worker per fuzz target so the gate is bounded by an input count rather than\\n1364:creation, clone, adoption, or any runtime capability. Schema acceptance alone\\n1374:  -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n1376:  -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n1378:  -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n1380:  -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3265,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 817,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
