{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":199,"recorded_at":1780531400000393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a733ae1f-f860-496a-b85c-9e2054e1de18"},"task_id":"a733ae1f-f860-496a-b85c-9e2054e1de18","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a733ae1f-f860-496a-b85c-9e2054e1de18","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(599 line(s) above)\n600|package mutates no durable state and keeps no cache, so it has no\n601|crash or idempotency surface.\n602|\n603|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n604|\n605|```bash\n606|go test ./internal/secprim -count=1\n607|go test ./internal/secprim -cover -count=1\n608|```\n609|\n610|## Security Conformance Test Instrument\n611|\n612|[`internal/secconftest`](internal/secconftest) is the test instrument\n613|for the Section 16 production gates above: deterministic fixture\n614|runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzz drivers, hostile\n615|strings, and platform capability skips. It decides nothing itself —\n616|every refusal stays in `secprim`, every grammar in\n617|[`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar), every bound check in\n618|[`internal/environ`](internal/environ) — and every mechanism ships\n619|with a proof that disabling it reddens the suite.\n620|\n621|The `Runner` executes named fixtures in sorted order over an explicit\n622|seed and folds names, reports, and production-call counts into one\n623|digest, with each component witnessed by a dedicated test (a\n624|report-only or name-only change reddens the suite); a fixture that\n625|records no production call is refused, so a corpus that never reaches\n626|the entry point cannot pass as coverage. `Fake` is a manually\n627|advanced clock that never reads the wall clock (a 20 ms sleep moves\n628|`time.Now` and not the fake), and the `Recording` wrapper makes an\n629|unwired clock read as zero calls — detected, not passed. The\n630|`Injector` arms five instrument-local `CR-MAT-*` phase boundaries\n631|(not the SPEC `CR-MAT-01..08` registry, whose names are refused as\n632|unknown) over a three-phase durable-commit model with the Section\n633|13.13 outcome vocabulary (`safe_retry`, `explicit_rollback`,\n634|`recoverable_parked_state`); identical retries return the\n635|byte-identical receipt while a changed body fails with\n636|`idempotency_mismatch` and stages nothing new, and finalization is\n637|terminal for clean and crashed `Commit` alike — a commit-apply fault\n638|fires after the durable write, so the operation counts as committed:\n639|further rollback is refused with the committed bytes intact\n640|(`AC-CLONE-005`), a second `Commit` names the terminal state, a\n641|`Prepare` past finalization is refused, and a pre-commit `Rollback`\n642|forgets the operation so a fresh `Prepare` restages the recovery\n643|retry. Every armed point is\n644|consumption-checked, so an arm the drive never reaches fails its\n645|test; all five points are driven through the `Transactor`, including\n646|rollback-enter. Eight `Fuzz*` targets drive the argv, member-path, env-name,\n647|redact, escape, render, guard-resolve, and case-collision entries\n648|through one shared `Driver` that seed-corpus tests prove reaches\n649|production (22 arrivals per entry); the env-name and redact targets\n650|additionally pin the poles a no-op gate fails (refused empty /\n651|admitted well-formed name; rewritten secret / passing innocuous\n652|line). Every target is registered in the configured validation\n653|matrix. The hostile roster derives 18 classes from the pinned\n654|specification text (every quote verified in its section) with members\n655|generated from Unicode tables and `scalar` predicates rather than the\n656|gates under test; every roster `Gate` is pinned and driven through\n657|the production entry it names, the bidi vocabulary is pinned\n658|rune-for-rune with corpus coverage, plus a symlink-escape commit\n659|witness gated on a probed capability. Capability probes (`symlink`,\n660|`fifo`, `mode-bits`, `nonroot`) each really attempt their\n661|capability — symlink create+Lstat, `mkfifo`+Lstat, `chmod 000`\n662|denial, uid check — and each gates a named test (symlink-escape\n663|commit witness, fifo byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits/nonroot denial\n664|test); they skip only where the platform cannot provide and fail on\n665|strict platforms where absence is unexpected (symlink and fifo are\n666|strict on linux and darwin, pinned exactly). `Require` takes a minimal\n667|testing handle so both the skip and the fail arms are driven through\n668|the real function with a recording fake; `TestMain` prints the\n669|process-wide report after every test, including the parallel ones.\n670|The per-test skip\n671|datum is the `--- SKIP` lines under `go test -v` (0 on darwin/arm64\n672|non-root); the final report line witnesses the counters after the\n673|whole suite, which honestly reads zero where every probe passes.\n674|\n675|Run the focused tests, race, coverage, and fuzz smoke with:\n676|\n677|```bash\n678|go test ./internal/secconftest -count=1\n679|go test ./internal/secconftest -race -count=1\n680|go test ./internal/secconftest -cover -count=1\n681|go test ./internal/secconftest -run='^$' -fuzz='^FuzzCheckArgv$' -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\n682|```\n683|\n684|Stated bounds: the commit model proves the injector and the outcome\n685|vocabulary, not any product recovery path; the crash-point names are\n686|instrument-local, not the SPEC registry, and a site added without an\n687|arm is outside the model. Fuzz covers the Section 16 string and\n688|vector gates, not containment races; the env-name/redact fuzz pins\n689|cover the no-op poles while the interior grammar and per-class\n690|markers stay with the hostile corpus; tombstone-deletion and TOCTOU\n691|shapes have no product surface in this story and are not driven. A\n692|skip-gated probe that reports unavailable on a non-strict platform\n693|skips by construction —\n694|the `--- SKIP` line is the signal, so CI watches skip counts rather\n695|than treating green as unskipped. Driver delegation to production is\n696|read-verified with arrival counts, not mutant-pinned. No new\n697|capability is advertised: the instrument cannot enable a platform\n698|lane or provider suite.\n699|\n700|## Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\n701|\n702|`.github/workflows/ci.yml` is the gate that decides what a green check\n703|means. Every job proves its selection matched something: a test selector,\n704|file scan, derivation, or matrix expansion that finds nothing fails closed\n705|instead of passing on an empty result set. No job declares a skip\n706|condition, so no job can skip quietly; the terminal verdict job additionally\n707|refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\n708|\n709|| Job | What runs | What green proves |\n710|| --- | --- | --- |\n711|| Contract preservation | `tracecheck`, catalog freshness, focused `internal/cigate` contract gates | The pinned lock and the generated catalog agree on every historical and current contract version, and each gate selection matched its named test |\n712|| Linters | `go vet`, Windows `go vet`, `gofmt` with a non-empty-scan guard | The tree type-checks on both GOOS values and carries no formatting drift |\n713|| Test | Full suite uncached | Every package passed; the run matched at least one package |\n714|| Race detector | Full suite under `-race` | No data race fired anywhere in the suite |\n715|| Coverage numbers | Full suite with `-cover`, percentages in the run summary | Per-package coverage was measured and reported; there is no floor, so coverage is a number, not a gate |\n716|| Conformance fixtures | Story suites on Ubuntu and macOS | Exact fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass per platform, with skip lines and the probe-counter line as evidence; crash/idempotency evidence comes from the Transactor battery in this matrix |\n717|| Fuzz smoke | Targets derived from the compiled test binary, each smoked briefly | Every derived target executed its engine, proven by its elapsed line rather than by exit status alone |\n718|| Unsupported-capability claim check | README scanned against live probe verdicts | No unsupported capability is advertised: mentions resolve to probe, skip, gate, or test context, never to a positive availability claim about an unavailable capability |\n719|| Windows compile-only | `GOOS=windows` build and vet, test files included | The tree compiles for Windows; green here never implies behaviour was executed there |\n720|| Gates verdict | Dependency-result check | Every gate above succeeded and none skipped |\n721|\n722|[`internal/cigate`](internal/cigate) holds the CI-facing gate library:\n723|contract-version agreement derived from `internal/specpin` and\n724|`internal/catalog` (a version either side cannot account for is refused),\n725|fuzz-target derivation from the instrument's own target map, and the\n726|advertisement check wired to the `internal/secconftest` probe set rather\n727|than to a second vocabulary. It ships no command by deliberation: its\n728|library reaches the embedded specification document through the\n729|instrument, which the `specdoc` guard reserves to the existing repository\n(more lines below)"}}}
