{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c60b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":352,"recorded_at":1780531400000699,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"call_id":"call_01a0782d0ac17061a52381f67798747f","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2uowwk/TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2uowwk — M0 CI and release gates\n2|\n3|Candidate tree OID: `7be8309b01f900f0162f1bc525e98ca857fcc853`\n4|\n5|Story: STORY-260830-1i3qu7 (security-primitives-and-conformance-ci), final leaf.\n6|Scope: AX v0.5.0 §16, §19.2–19.5, §20.2, Appendix D. Work stays inside the\n7|story boundary: `internal/secprim` and `internal/secconftest` production code\n8|are untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim internal/secconftest` empty\n9|except nothing — verified clean), and no foreign guard was weakened.\n10|\n11|## What changed\n12|\n13|- New `internal/cigate`: CI-facing gate library (doc/contracts/claims/targets\n14|  + contracts/claims/targets tests). No `main` package by deliberation (see\n15|  Bounds).\n16|- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: 1 job → 10 jobs, each fail-closed on empty\n17|  matches, no conditional skips, terminal `gates-verdict` refusing any\n18|  non-success dependency.\n19|- `README.md`: \"Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\" section (scanner-clean,\n20|  no counts published except stable job structure).\n21|- `LOGBOOK.md`: 2248 entry (findings, decision, evidence).\n22|\n23|## AC coverage: 11 of 11 rows driven\n24|\n25|| # | AC row | Production entry point | Named committed test |\n26|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n27|| 1 | historical (v0.4.3) contract preservation runs in CI | `cigate.VerifyContractPreservation` → `specpin.Current` + `catalog.ForRelease(v0.4.3)` | `TestVerifyContractPreservationLive` |\n28|| 2 | current (v0.5.0) contract preservation runs in CI | `cigate.VerifyContractPreservation` → `specpin.Current` + `catalog.ForRelease(v0.5.0)` | `TestVerifyContractPreservationLive`, `TestDerivedSetsAreComplete` |\n29|| 3 | linters run in CI | `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet`, `gofmt` (workflow) | `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` pins vet literals; gofmt guard proven red (§Red) |\n30|| 4 | race tests run in CI | `go test -race ./...` (workflow race job) | full suite green under `-race`; `-race` proven rejecting (§Red) |\n31|| 5 | coverage runs in CI | `go test ./... -cover` (workflow coverage job, numbers only, no floor) | 22 `coverage:` lines; missing-package fails (§Red) |\n32|| 6 | fixture matrices run in CI | os×package matrix (`secprim`, `secconftest`); `-list`-derived fuzz loop | `TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted`, matrix `--- PASS` guards, per-target `fuzz: elapsed` guard |\n33|| 7 | unsupported-capability claim check runs in CI | `cigate.CheckAdvertisements` over README with `cigate.ProbeStates` | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim`, `TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted` |\n34|| 8 | exact contract fixtures pass | `secprim.CheckMemberPath/CheckArgv/IsEnvName/EscapeForTerminal/Redact` via hostile corpus | `TestHostilePathMembersRefused`, `TestHostileMemberCounts` (17 classes + counts), `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction` |\n35|| 9 | negative/refusal cases pass | same gates, refusal arms | `TestHostileGatesAreWired`, `TestQuoteInSectionRefusals`, `TestRunnerRefusesUnreachedFixture` |\n36|| 10 | crash/idempotency evidence (durable-state operations) | `secconftest.Transactor` (Prepare/Commit/Rollback) in matrix | `TestTransactorIdempotentRetry`, `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`, `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize`; `cigate` itself is read-only (stated bound) |\n37|| 11 | no unsupported capability advertised | `cigate.CheckAdvertisements` + live `secconftest` probes | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` (all-unavailable posture), probe-counter line in CI |\n38|\n39|## Mutant battery: 13 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL; 11 killed, 2 survived with bounds\n40|\n41|Harness: `/tmp/mutant-harness.sh` (kept outside the worktree for re-runs);\n42|per-mutant logs `/tmp/mutant-<id>.log`; results `/tmp/mutant-results.tsv`.\n43|Each mutant reverted and verified byte-identical after its run.\n44|\n45|| Mutant | Class | What it narrows the gate to | Named test that fails | Result |\n46|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n47|| N1 verb-drop (`available`) | narrowing | admits the available-claim | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused` (+ `TestFindingCarriesLine`) | killed |\n48|| N2 negation-drop (`not`) | narrowing | refuses the honestly negated sentence | `TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted` | killed |\n49|| N3 boundary-drop (substring match) | narrowing | admits `protest`-style token-preserving mention | `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker` | killed |\n50|| N4 version-order-blind | narrowing | admits reordered versions | `TestCheckAgreementRefusals/version_order_changed` | killed |\n51|| N5 case-narrow (no folding) | narrowing | admits capitalised `Available` / `No` | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused`, `TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted` | killed |\n52|| A1 positive arm off | arm-deletion | admits marked positive claims | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused` | killed |\n53|| A2 unclassified arm off | arm-deletion | admits unmarked neutral mentions | `TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused` | killed |\n54|| A3 empty guards off | arm-deletion | passes on empty vocabulary/document | `TestEmptyInputsAreRefused` | killed |\n55|| A4 catalog-extra direction off | arm-deletion | admits catalog-only contracts | `TestCheckAgreementRefusals` | killed |\n56|| A5 target guards off | arm-deletion | admits malformed/empty derivation | `TestSortedTargetsRefusals` | killed |\n57|| A6 root comparison off | arm-deletion | admits one-sided release rename | `TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift` | killed |\n58|| C1 release order swap | census-only | — (verdict is order-free) | — survives | survived: iteration order is presentation; agreement is keyed, tests assert sets |\n59|| C2 finding order reverse | census-only | — (verdict is order-free) | — survives | survived: emission order is presentation; mixed test asserts refusal sets |\n60|\n61|Superseded during the run: N3-v1 (drop one marker) survived because the\n62|marker arm covers every live sentence redundantly — not a hole. Replaced with\n63|the true narrowing mutant above. A5-v1/v2 did not compile (Go unused rules);\n64|v3 keeps both names referenced behind `false` and is killed by test.\n65|\n66|## Deliberate red per job (all observed, real exit codes)\n67|\n68|| Job | Failing input | Observed |\n69|| --- | --- | --- |\n70|| contract-preservation | `-run TestDoesNotExist` exits 0; `--- PASS` guard exits 1 | selector green on empty, guard red — the class this job exists to catch |\n71|| contract-preservation | `tracecheck -section bogus` | exit 1 (`invalid assigned section`) |\n72|| contract-preservation | version-drop/reorder/extra mutants | killed (battery N4/A4/A6) |\n73|| lint | scratch `gofmt`-dirty file | listed (exit 0) → `test -z` guard exit 1 |\n74|| test/race | scratch data-race module under `-race` | `WARNING: DATA RACE`, exit 1 |\n75|| coverage | `go test ./internal/does-not-exist -cover` | exit 1 (setup failed) |\n76|| fixture-matrix | empty target list to `test -s` | exit 1 |\n77|| fuzz-smoke | `-fuzz='^NoSuchTarget$'` exits 0 with \"no fuzz tests to fuzz\" | `^fuzz: elapsed` guard exit 1; real target guard exit 0 |\n78|| capability-claims | claim appended to real README | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` FAIL (README restored byte-clean) |\n79|| windows-compile-only | scratch `syscall.Mkfifo` under `GOOS=windows` | exit 1 (`undefined: syscall.Mkfifo`) |\n80|| gates-verdict | simulated `{\"lint\": {\"result\": \"skipped\"}}` | `jq -e` exit 1; all-success exit 0 |\n81|\n82|## Gates (final tree, exit codes)\n83|\n84|- `go test ./... -count=1` → exit 0, 22 packages ok, 0 FAIL\n85|- `go test -race ./... -count=1` → exit 0, 22 ok (three sweeps; re-run on final tree)\n86|- `go test ./... -cover -count=1` → exit 0, 22 `coverage:` lines, 0 `no test files` (cigate 90.5%)\n87|- `go vet ./...` → exit 0; `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` → exit 0; `GOOS=windows go build ./...` → exit 0\n88|- `gofmt -l internal` → empty; `go generate ./internal/catalog` + diff → clean\n89|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` → exit 0 (contracts=60, compatibility=55, cases=94, unchanged)\n90|- `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` → PASS (caught and fixed a dropped `go build ./...` mid-work)\n91|\n92|## Bounds and follow-ups for the orchestrator (prose, no board elements created)\n93|\n94|1. Availability is host-local: a positive claim about a here-available\n95|   capability is admitted. Cross-host claim truth is outside the gate.\n96|2. Coverage has no floor by requirement; adding one needs its own observed\n97|   rejection first.\n98|3. Windows green means compiled+vetted, never executed. macOS/Windows hosted\n99|   execution beyond the fixture matrix (provider suites, §19.3–19.4\n100|   lifecycle) belongs to later stories with real lanes.\n101|4. `task-board.config.json` validation commands were not extended: no new\n102|   Fuzz targets were added, so `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget`\n103|   still covers all 8.\n104|5. Suggested (not created): a follow-up leaf owning hosted macOS/Windows\n105|   lane evidence and the §19.5 release-acceptance checklist when product\n106|   lanes exist.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
