{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c64f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":386,"recorded_at":1780531400000767,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"472ecfa4-fb18-40fd-9311-cf0a2e5c838a"},"task_id":"472ecfa4-fb18-40fd-9311-cf0a2e5c838a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"472ecfa4-fb18-40fd-9311-cf0a2e5c838a","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2uowwk/TASK-260830-2uowwk_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2uowwk — review verdict, CR revision 1 (`story_final`)\n2|\n3|**Verdict: changes_requested → `to-dev`.**\n4|**repeat-of: none** (revision 1 of this element; F1 and F5 recur across earlier\n5|leaves of this Story, see \"Cross-leaf recurrence\").\n6|\n7|Reviewed tree: `67eea42b99fdfd5b40ccba311545d49ae50a1010` (CR candidate), base\n8|`157a54cfe4e952a2638b574230967989178e9a05`. Worktree verified byte-identical to\n9|the candidate tree before and after every probe below (`CLAUDE.md` reports a\n10|false diff under content hashing — it is mode `120000` → `AGENTS.md`).\n11|\n12|No gate in the new code admits what it must reject. I attacked all eleven\n13|G-A/G-B/G-C surfaces and every one held. What does not hold is a set of five\n14|advertised behaviours that do not reproduce — on a Story whose own AC row is\n15|*no unsupported capability is advertised*. All five fixes are localized and\n16|touch no gate logic.\n17|\n18|---\n19|\n20|## Blocking findings\n21|\n22|### F1 — `capability-claims` advertises live probe verdicts it never reads\n23|\n24|`.github/workflows/ci.yml:293-298`, step **\"Record live probe verdicts\"**.\n25|\n26|The step runs `go test ./internal/secconftest -run 'TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts'`.\n27|That test records two *synthetic* verdicts, asserts `Report()` moved, and restores\n28|the counters in `t.Cleanup` (`internal/secconftest/skip_test.go:238-246`). It\n29|invokes `Require` for no real capability. The line the step then greps is printed\n30|by `TestMain` *after* the restore, so it is `skipped=0 \"\" failed=0 \"\"` by\n31|construction on every host.\n32|\n33|Reproduced:\n34|\n35|| Command | Last `capabilities on` line |\n36|| --- | --- |\n37|| the step verbatim (`-run 'TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts'`) | `secconftest capabilities on darwin: skipped=0 \"\" failed=0 \"\"` |\n38|| full suite (`go test ./internal/secconftest -v`) | `secconftest capabilities on darwin: skipped=0 \"\" failed=0 \"\"` |\n39|| **nothing at all** (`-run='^$' -fuzz='^FuzzNoSuchTarget$'`) | `secconftest capabilities on darwin: skipped=0 \"\" failed=0 \"\"` |\n40|\n41|Three runs, one of which executed zero tests, are indistinguishable. The line\n42|cannot separate \"every probe available\" from \"no probe ran\". The step is also\n43|non-gating: `grep ... | tail -n 1` takes `tail`'s status, so it exits 0\n44|unconditionally and can never redden the job.\n45|\n46|The frozen leaf already forbids exactly this reading, in `Report()`'s own doc\n47|comment (`internal/secconftest/skip.go`): *\"Citing a Report line as host evidence\n48|is only honest for verdicts the suite really recorded; the per-test skip datum is\n49|the `--- SKIP` lines under `go test -v`.\"* The `fixture-matrix` job does it the\n50|honest way; this job does not.\n51|\n52|The claim is then carried into two artifacts:\n53|- `README.md` gate table: \"README scanned against **live probe verdicts**\";\n54|- `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` AC row 11: production entry point\n55|  \"`cigate.CheckAdvertisements` + **live** `secconftest` probes\", evidence\n56|  \"probe-counter line in CI\".\n57|\n58|Neither reproduces. `ProbeState.Available` is computed from a real probe and then\n59|discarded by every consumer in the repository: `ProbeStates()` is called only from\n60|`CapabilityIDs()` (`internal/cigate/claims.go:139`), which returns IDs and drops\n61|availability. Every `CheckAdvertisements` call site — production and test — passes\n62|a forced state (`allUnavailable`/`availableStates`, `claims_test.go:246,261`).\n63|\n64|To be explicit about merit: forcing all probes unavailable is *stronger* than\n65|scanning against live verdicts, and host-independent. The design is right. Only\n66|the description is wrong, in three places, and the CI step dressed as evidence\n67|records none.\n68|\n69|**Fix:** either make the step run a suite that actually probes and assert\n70|something about the result, or delete it and stop citing a probe-counter line;\n71|correct the README row and AC row 11 to say the gate scans with every probe\n72|forced unavailable.\n73|\n74|### F2 — outcome document names a tree that does not contain the work\n75|\n76|`TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` line 3: `Candidate tree OID: 7be8309b01f900f0162f1bc525e98ca857fcc853`.\n77|\n78|That is exactly `git rev-parse HEAD^{tree}` — the tree *before* this leaf. It\n79|carries **zero** of the ten changed files and no `internal/cigate` entry at all\n80|(`git ls-tree -r 7be8309b -- internal/cigate` → 0 rows; the CR tree has 7). The\n81|document's own numbers are impossible on the tree it names: `cigate 90.5%`\n82|cannot be measured in a tree with no `cigate` package. `git write-tree` returns\n83|`7be8309b` here because `internal/cigate` is untracked, so the index tree omits it.\n84|\n85|The record's tree is `67eea42b…`; `git diff 7be8309b 67eea42b` is the entire leaf\n86|delta, 10 files / +1474.\n87|\n88|The measurements themselves are sound — I reproduced them below on the correct\n89|tree. The defect is the provenance line, and this is the check the round brief\n90|named as having failed in two earlier leaves of this programme.\n91|\n92|**Fix:** `resource update` the document with `67eea42b99fdfd5b40ccba311545d49ae50a1010`.\n93|\n94|### F3 — `cigate.FuzzTargets` claims a CI wiring that does not exist\n95|\n96|`internal/cigate/targets.go:12`: *\"CI iterates this derivation rather than a\n97|retyped copy.\"* CI does not. `fuzz-smoke` derives from `go test -list 'Fuzz'`\n98|(`ci.yml:243`); `FuzzTargets` appears nowhere in `ci.yml` and has no non-test\n99|caller in the repository. It is reachable only from `TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted`.\n100|\n101|`doc.go:17-18` repeats the claim as one of the package's three stated purposes.\n102|\n103|The `-list` derivation is arguably the better one (it reads the compiled binary),\n104|so no gate is missing — but a guard whose doc asserts a production wiring it does\n105|not have is the shape this Story exists to refuse.\n106|\n107|**Fix:** either wire `fuzz-smoke` through `FuzzTargets`, or drop the function and\n108|its two doc claims.\n109|\n110|---\n111|\n112|## Unstated bounds (fix by stating, not by widening)\n113|\n114|### F4 — the advertisement scanner only sees backticked IDs\n115|\n116|`CheckAdvertisements` matches ``\"`\"+id+\"`\"`` (`claims.go:241`). With every probe\n117|forced unavailable, all of these are **admitted**:\n118|\n119|| Planted sentence | Findings |\n120|| --- | ---: |\n121|| ``The `fifo` capability is available on Windows.`` | 1 (refused — gate works) |\n122|| `FIFO creation is available and supported on Windows.` | 0 |\n123|| `The fifo capability is available on Windows.` | 0 |\n124|| ``There is no doubt that `fifo` is available on Windows.`` | 0 |\n125|| ``It is not false that `fifo` is supported on Windows.`` | 0 |\n126|| ``Only good news: `fifo` is available on Windows.`` | 0 |\n127|\n128|Rows 4–6 are inside the bound `doc.go` does state (\"it classifies sentences, not\n129|intent\"). Rows 2–3 are not: the backtick requirement appears only in the `Finding`\n130|struct comment, while `doc.go`'s **Stated bounds** paragraph omits it and the\n131|README says \"**mentions** resolve to probe, skip, gate, or test context\" — which\n132|reads as all mentions. An unbackticked capability advertisement is invisible.\n133|\n134|### F5 — `fuzz-smoke` is scoped to one package, described as \"derived targets\"\n135|\n136|The job derives 8 targets from `internal/secconftest` only. Five further real\n137|targets exist outside it — `internal/canonicaljson` (4) and `internal/scalar` (1) —\n138|and are never smoked. `doc.go:17` asserts \"fuzz entry points stay in\n139|internal/secconftest\", which is false repo-wide. Story-scope coverage is complete\n140|and their seed corpora do run under the `test` job, so this is a bound to state,\n141|not a gap to close in this leaf.\n142|\n143|---\n144|\n145|## Non-blocking observation\n146|\n147|**Verb-drop battery dies by bookkeeping, not behaviour.** `positiveAvailability`\n148|has 5 members; the mutant table ships one drop mutant (N1, `available`). I\n149|censused all five:\n150|\n151|| Dropped verb | Suite | Killed by |\n152|| --- | --- | --- |\n153|| `available` | red | count guard **+** `TestFindingCarriesLine` (behavioural) |\n154|| `supported` | red | count guard only |\n155|| `enabled` | red | count guard only |\n156|| `works` | red | count guard only |\n157|| `passes` | red | count guard only |\n158|\n159|`claims_test.go:57` `t.Fatalf`s on `len(claims)-1 != len(positiveAvailability)`,\n160|which aborts the parent before any subtest runs — 0 of 5 behavioural subtests\n161|fire under any drop. Every mutant is still killed and the DoD letter is met, and\n162|in the green state all six subtests do drive their verb\n163|(`--- PASS: TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused/{available,supported,enabled,works,passes,capital}`).\n164|Only the kill *mechanism* is thin. Not blocking; worth a line in the table.\n165|\n166|---\n167|\n168|## What I attacked and could not break\n169|\n170|| Probe | Result |\n171|| --- | --- |\n172|| **G-A** empty test selector (`-run TestDoesNotExist`) | `go test` exits **0**; the `--- PASS` grep loop fires → job red. Guard load-bearing. |\n173|| **G-A** empty fuzz derivation (`-list 'ZZZNoSuchFuzz'`) | `grep` 1, `test -s` **1** → job red |\n174|| **G-A** `-fuzz='^FuzzNoSuchTarget$'` | exits **0** (\"no fuzz tests to fuzz\"); `^fuzz: elapsed` guard exits 1 → job red. Real target: guard exits 0, engine ran. |\n175|| **G-A** `needs` completeness | 10 jobs, 9 non-verdict, **all 9 in `needs`**, none extra |\n176|| **G-A** timeouts | all 10 jobs carry `timeout-minutes` (5–15) |\n177|| **G-A** skip surface | exactly one `if:` in the file, `always()` on `gates-verdict` |\n178|| **G-A** aggregator | drove the `jq` over synthetic states: `success`→admit; `skipped`/`failure`/`cancelled`/`null`→**reject**. Empty `{}` admits, unreachable (`needs` is static and complete). |\n179|| **G-B** version set derived, not listed | `checkReleaseRoots(specpin.ReleaseV050/V043, catalog.ReleaseV050/V043)`; no version literal in `ci.yml` |\n180|| **G-B** alter a historical contract | dropped `2.0.0` from the v0.4.3 Mesh RPC override → `TestVerifyContractPreservationLive` + `TestDerivedSetsAreComplete` **FAIL**, `normative source pin mismatch: v0.4.3 version overrides drift`; 2 of 6 PASS guards fire |\n181|| **G-B** stale generated catalog | drifted `catalog.v0.5.0.json` (`checkpoint_id`→`mutant_id`) → freshness step exits **1** |\n182|| **G-B** token-preserving generator disarm | `//go:generate`→`// go:generate` + drifted input → freshness step exits 0. **Pre-existing at HEAD** (identical step in the old `verify` job), and this leaf's new gate *strengthens* it: with the directive disarmed, a contract-version drift in `catalog_gen.go` is still caught by `VerifyContractPreservation`. Not charged to this CR. |\n183|| **G-C** vocabulary source | `CapabilityIDs`→`ProbeStates`→`secconftest.DefaultCapabilities()`. No second vocabulary. |\n184|| **G-C** make it fail | planted ``The `fifo` capability is available on Windows.`` in the real README → `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` **FAIL**, reason `positive availability claim for an unavailable capability`; README restored byte-clean |\n185|| **G-D** coverage | no floor, and job name + comment + README all say so. Honest report, not a gate. |\n186|| **G-D** windows | `GOOS=windows go build`/`go vet` only; nothing in the file executes a Windows binary; job name and comment both disclaim execution |\n187|| **G-E** landability | `origin/main` == `157a54c` == CR base; `origin/main` is an ancestor of HEAD; 2 commits ahead |\n188|| **G-E** signatures | `722ed1a`, `7f90e58` both `Good \"git\" signature for oparin@me.com` |\n189|| **G-E** frozen leaves | `git diff 722ed1a…67eea42b -- internal/secprim` empty; `git diff 7f90e58…67eea42b -- internal/secconftest` empty |\n190|| **G-E** first-push risk | `actions/checkout@v7` and `actions/setup-go@v7` both resolve (unchanged from HEAD); CI green on `main` |\n191|\n192|## Suites re-run on the candidate tree (this session, macOS/darwin arm64, go1.25.5)\n193|\n194|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n195|| --- | ---: | --- |\n196|| `go test ./... -v -count=1` | 0 | 22 `^ok`, 0 `^FAIL`, 1352 `--- PASS`, 1 `--- SKIP` (`TestDumpSweepSites`) |\n197|| `go test -race ./... -count=1` | 0 | 22 `^ok`, no `DATA RACE`, 125s |\n198|| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | 22 `coverage:` lines, 0 `no test files`, `cigate 90.5%` |\n199|| `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` | 0 | clean |\n200|| `gofmt -l internal` | — | empty |\n201|| `go test ./internal/cigate -v` | 0 | 20 PASS / 0 FAIL |\n202|\n203|`-race`, `-cover` and package coverage match the producer's `verify.log` exactly.\n204|\n205|## Cross-leaf recurrence\n206|\n207|F2 is the third occurrence in this programme of \"outcome document names a tree\n208|the record does not carry\". F1 is the second occurrence of \"a counter that host\n209|conditions cannot move, cited as host evidence\" — the first was fixed in\n210|TASK-260830-7a0s2c by adding `TestMain`, and this leaf re-introduces the same\n211|constancy by narrowing `-run` so no writer runs. If a third arrives, the next\n212|step is a gate, not another revision."}}}
