{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":467,"recorded_at":1780531400000929,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5f5ae665-3077-4f81-a472-599efc464760"},"task_id":"5f5ae665-3077-4f81-a472-599efc464760","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5f5ae665-3077-4f81-a472-599efc464760","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; grep -n \\\"checklist\\\\|\\\\\\\\- \\\\\\\\[\\\" \\\"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/EPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-1i3qu7_security-primitives-and-conformance-ci/TASK-260830-2uowwk_establish-m0-ci-and-release-gates/progress.md\\\" | head; echo ===; head -30 \\\"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/EPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-1i3qu7_security-primitives-and-conformance-ci/TASK-260830-2uowwk_establish-m0-ci-and-release-gates/progress.md\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK format and task progress\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\\n- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\\n- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\\n- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n- FIX: `census_test.go` used `specdoc` without deriving from it (vet failure on the unused import). Added `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` (20 closed bodies: every Required list in document order plus the Members map as a set, with the success/failure envelopes derived by the spec's own first-four-fields rule, the manifest from its table's first-column spans, and the doctor result from the operation table) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` (16 vocabularies pinned to their spec unions; operation/capability registries in order, value sets as sets).\\n- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 5: B4/B5 closed as classes by derived denominators, N8 indirection refused\\n- FIX (B8): `bound_census_test.go` rosters all 97 production bound sites (six helpers by member, len guards by shape with values normalized out, DecodeFindings cap instantiations): 82 driven at entries both edges, 15 exempt (4 mechanism, 4 plumbing, 3 equivalent, 5 stated-bound 65536-count rows). `requireStringBounds`/`requireUint53Bounds` wrappers are mechanism rows; the 19 caller sites carry the rows.\\n- FIX (B7): `identity_census_test.go` rosters all 62 `X != Y` gates (mechanical classes excluded) plus a 5-row presence census with structural proof: 54 driven zero-on-exempted-side at exported entries (CheckProbe x6 both sides, seal 8x2, admission key x5 entry+binding sides, binding caller-side x4), 8 exempt (2 dispatch, 4 sentinel, 2 equivalent).\\n- FIX (N8): `constructorSitesInFile` reports any `axerror.New` selector outside call-fun position; synthetic proof covers package-level and function-local indirection (report) vs definition spelling and Decode (exempt).\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): `Bext-min` is genuinely equivalent (no 2-char key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar); `Iops-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n===\\n23:- [x] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Run historical/current contract preservation, linters, race tests, coverage, fixture matrices, and unsupported-capability claim checks in CI\\n24:- [x] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\n25:- [x] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\n26:- [x] Code written per task description and AC\\n27:- [x] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\n28:- [x] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\n29:- [x] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\n30:- [x] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\n31:- [x] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\n32:- [x] Lint clean\\n===\\n## Status\\ndevelopment\\n\\n## Review\\nrequired\\n\\n## Task Class\\ncode\\n\\n## Estimate\\nestimated(fibonacci(8))\\n\\n## Blocked By\\n- TASK-260830-7a0s2c\\n\\n## Blocks\\n- TASK-260830-35urbp\\n- TASK-260830-2bnr39\\n- TASK-260830-2u34k1\\n- TASK-260830-355gon\\n\\n## Checklist\\n- [x] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Run historical/current contract preservation, linters, race tests, coverage, fixture matrices, and unsupported-capability claim checks in CI\\n- [x] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\n- [x] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\n- [x] Code written per task description and AC\\n- [x] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\n- [x] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\n- [x] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\n- [x] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 17460,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4365,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
