{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cca3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":1196,"recorded_at":1780531400002387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"db2ac1b8-a3f3-4273-a52c-28d8ee90f066"},"task_id":"db2ac1b8-a3f3-4273-a52c-28d8ee90f066","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"db2ac1b8-a3f3-4273-a52c-28d8ee90f066","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-39-1\",\n  \"command\": \"test \\\"$(go test ./internal/secconftest -list '^Fuzz' 2>/dev/null | grep -c '^Fuzz')\\\" -eq 99; echo \\\"wrong-count-pin exit=$?\\\"; sed -n '1,20p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Count-guard red proof, LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"wrong-count-pin exit=1\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 2248 — CI gates leaf: cigate library, ten-job workflow, no new main\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk (final leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New `internal/cigate` (doc/contracts/claims/targets + 3 test files, no `main`); `.github/workflows/ci.yml` 1 job → 10; README \\\"Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\\\" section. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched; no foreign guard weakened.\\n- DECISION: no new `main` package. First Rosewood `cmd/cigate` tripped `TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary` + `TestModuleHasNoProductCommandYet` (lib reaches specdoc via secconftest). Widening that allowlist would self-mint an exemption, so the command was deleted; CI drives gates through focused name-guarded `go test -run` selections instead. Recorded in `internal/cigate/doc.go`.\\n- FINDING: `go test -fuzz='^NoSuch$'` exits 0 (\\\"no fuzz tests to fuzz\\\"). Fuzz-smoke step therefore requires the `^fuzz: elapsed` line per target, proven both directions (real 0, bogus 1).\\n- FINDING: existing `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` pins four literals in ci.yml; the rewrite initially dropped `go build ./...` and used non-verbose test. Restored: native Build step + `go test ./... -v -count=1`. The guard worked as designed.\\n- FINDING: N3-v1 mutant (drop one marker) survived — marker arm has redundancy by construction, not a hole. Replaced with boundary-anchoring narrowing (substring match), killed by new `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker`.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` (11/11 AC rows, 13-row mutant table, per-job red proofs with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants.log`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race ./...` exit 0 (22 ok x3 sweeps), `-cover` exit 0 (22 lines, cigate 90.5%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60/55 contracts, unchanged). Mutants 13 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL, 11 killed (5 narrowing + 6 arm-deletion), 2 census survivors with bounds (order-only).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2155 — secconftest round-3 rework: crashed commit counts as committed, Require wiring pinned, LOGBOOK corrected\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1/C1b/C2/C2b blocking + 7 unbounded survivors). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (commit-apply fault finalizes with parked receipt, `ErrPreparePastFinalize`/`ErrCommitPastFinalize`, rollback forgets, staged-missing naming), `skip.go` (`requireT` interface), `main_test.go` (new, `TestMain` final report), `doc.go` (terminal + wiring bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched.\\n- C1 RULE: a crashed commit counts as committed — the durable write already happened, so rollback is forbidden (`ErrRollbackPastFinalize`) and bytes survive; recovery is via `CommittedBytes`/operator. Driven by `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`. C1b neighbours all named (no ENOENT inheritance): rollback-twice, commit-twice, commit-after-rollback, prepare-after-commit refused; prepare-after-rollback restages. Fifth crash point armed through the Transactor (P7 closed).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3329,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 833,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
