{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccc7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":1214,"recorded_at":1780531400002423,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f2770037-45b3-4dd5-ae2a-080876a23b90"},"task_id":"f2770037-45b3-4dd5-ae2a-080876a23b90","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f2770037-45b3-4dd5-ae2a-080876a23b90","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-06\n-\n-### 2248 — CI gates leaf: cigate library, ten-job workflow, no new main\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk rework (review-verdict-rev1, F1–F5 blocking + verb-battery observation). `internal/cigate` + `.github/workflows/ci.yml` + README. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched (restored byte-identical after two probe mutants; `git status` clean on both).\n+- F1: deleted the `Record live probe verdicts` step — it ran a synthetic-verdict test and grepped a constant line through a non-gating pipe. CI now scans the README with every probe forced unavailable (stronger than live scanning, host-independent); README table and `cigate/doc.go` say so, and the workflow comment states `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\n+- F3: wired, not deleted. New `TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` holds `go test -list ^Fuzz` output equal to `FuzzTargets()`; CI's fuzz-smoke runs it name-guarded before smoking. Entry-drop mutant kills both the derivation test and `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction`.\n+- F5: fuzz-smoke now derives per package over `secconftest` + `canonicaljson` + `scalar` (8+4+1=13, count pinned), each smoked with the `^fuzz: elapsed` guard — all 13 observed locally. `doc.go` no longer claims entry points stay in one package.\n+- F4: backtick bound stated in `doc.go` Stated bounds and the README row, pinned by `TestUnbacktickedProseIsOutsideTheScanner` (bare-prose positive claims admitted). Backtick-widening mutant killed by that test and by the real-README gate (bare `fifo` in prose gets refused).\n+- BATTERY: verb/negation size `Fatalf`s replaced by per-row behavioural kills + `battery-covers-gate` censuses. Three rewritten negation rows (`n't`, `pending`, `unless`) each previously hid behind a second negation. Censused drops: 5/5 verbs and 13/13 negations kill in their own subtest (spot-verified `supported`, `pending`; `available` also trips `TestFindingCarriesLine` by shared sentence).\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` rev2 (11/11 AC rows, 30-mutant battery, per-job red proofs) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants-rev2.log` + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_verify-rev2.log`. Full suite 22 ok, `-race` 22 ok, `-cover` 22 lines (cigate 90.5%), vet both GOOS, gofmt, catalog freshness, `tracecheck` all exit 0.\n+- NOTE (pre-existing, not fixed here): catalog-freshness step defeated by `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` (token preserved); at HEAD before this leaf. The contract-version gate still catches version drift with the directive disarmed.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 2248 — CI gates leaf: cigate library, ten-job workflow, no new main\n"}}}
