{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf41","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0782c-6f74-7fc3-a546-73229f09b865"},"sequence":1531,"recorded_at":1780531400003057,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d5642b5c-8a5c-4554-a722-903669c33bb0"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Rev2 rework is ready for review (handed off to review, `to-review`, checklist 18/18).\n\nWhat changed, per finding:\n\n- F1: deleted the `Record live probe verdicts` step — it ran a synthetic-verdict test and grepped a constant line through a non-gating pipe. The `capability-claims` job now scans the README with every probe forced unavailable; README table, `doc.go`, and the workflow comment all describe that posture, including that `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\n- F2: outcome doc now names `8d8231ac…`, computed via a temp index (real index untouched) and verified before naming — 7 `cigate` entries, exactly the 10 changed files.\n- F3: wired, not deleted. New `TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` holds `go test -list ^Fuzz` equal to `FuzzTargets()`; CI runs it name-guarded before smoking. An entry-drop mutant kills it and the seed pin.\n- F4: backtick bound stated in `doc.go` Stated bounds and the README row, pinned by `TestUnbacktickedProseIsOutsideTheScanner`; a backtick-widening mutant is killed by it and by the real-README gate.\n- F5: fuzz-smoke derives over `secconftest` + `canonicaljson` + `scalar` (8+4+1=13, count pinned), all 13 smoked locally with `^fuzz: elapsed` observed.\n- Battery: size `Fatalf`s replaced by behavioural subtest kills plus `battery-covers-gate` censuses; three negation rows rewritten to isolate one negation each.\n\nEvidence: 30 mutants applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL — 28 killed (5